  - consent-gated processing
  - medicine reference data
  - deterministic intent routing
  - bilingual software
abstract: >-
  Medora joins bilingual patient-held records, booking, and consent-gated
  assistive workflows. A historical deployed medicine reference remains distinct
  from the 44,226-row public S4/S5 reconstruction with row and field provenance.
  The combined optional detector/source bundle uses AGPL-3.0; publisher MIT and
  CC BY 4.0 notices remain attached to the medicine inputs. Private prescription
  images are excluded. Fixture and component results do not establish clinical
  effectiveness, national medicine-register completeness, or device approval.
